        <mxCell id="4KatQqS_aaxpho2ztIxi-7" value="&lt;div&gt;In AKS, a &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;service oftype&amp;nbsp;LoadBalancer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;automatically creates a&amp;nbsp;NodePort&amp;nbsp;and configures an Azure Load Balancer to route traffic to this port.&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;NodePort&amp;nbsp;field:&lt;/span&gt; indicates the port on each node in the cluster that has been opened to expose the service. Here’s a breakdown of the relevant parts:&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;The load balancerforwards the traffic to port&amp;nbsp;31836 on one of the nodes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;E&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;xternalAccess:&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;NodePort&amp;nbsp;allows external traffic to access a service running inside the AKS cluster by opening a specific port on all nodes in the cluster.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cluster-wide Access:The same port is opened on every node in the cluster, and traffic sent to thisport on any node is forwarded to the service.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Architects Daughter;align=left;fontSize=35;" parent="WfwI8hsEHnIwHEpeUaaj-80" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-450" y="-1010" width="1710" height="580" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
