        <mxCell id="8G45v4QA7ZbLvMoKy6Ll-34" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dual Stack Networking : NOtes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 102);&quot;&gt;Use case:&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-align: left; text-wrap: wrap; background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Use Case: IPv6 adoption is increasing, and dual-stack networking ensures that your applications are ready for the future where IPv6 might become more prevalent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left; font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 204, 153);&quot;&gt;Requires &lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;Kubenet &lt;/span&gt;networking or CNI OVerlay Plugin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left; font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;Dual-stack in required on the Azure virtual network&lt;/span&gt; and POD CiDR, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 204, 153);&quot;&gt;Single IPv6 only not supported&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left; font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;If using Kubenet - Azure route table limit of &lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;400 routes per table&lt;/span&gt;, each node requires two routes -on per IP famliy so eseentially the limit is 200 routes so 200 nodes&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 37px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=37;fontFamily=Architects Daughter;labelBackgroundColor=none;" parent="jg9sSwiCN6oEBZTyevX6-7" vertex="1">
