        <mxCell id="YLipig3j6BaiT96UUwU8-106" value="&lt;font color=&quot;#009900&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 35px;&quot;&gt;10.244.0.0/16&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=35;fontFamily=Courier New;fontColor=#000000;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=3;" parent="jg9sSwiCN6oEBZTyevX6-7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1330" y="480" width="300" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oLPVPFHUQ2T455JdV-RN-1" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &amp;quot;Architects Daughter&amp;quot;; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: center; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: nowrap; background-color: rgb(251, 251, 251); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; float: none; display: inline !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 36px;&quot;&gt;fd12:3456:789a::/48&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="jg9sSwiCN6oEBZTyevX6-7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1380" y="40" width="350" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oqalSY3rHp3BdiXpaR-A-9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual Stack Support with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual stack support in AKS allows clusters to use both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, enabling seamless communication across different IP families. This is particularly useful for applications that need to operate in environments where both IP versions are required.Prepares your infrastructure for future IPv6 adoption.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Key Features&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual IP Families:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Supports both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses for pods and services.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Ensures compatibility with modern networking requirements.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Enhanced Networking:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Provides better network isolation and security.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Facilitates communication in hybrid environments.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Scalability:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Allows for larger address spaces, accommodating more pods and services.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Reduces the risk of IP address exhaustion.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Limitations of Dual Stack Support with AKS&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;While dual stack support in Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) offers many benefits, there are some limitations and considerations to be aware of:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Cluster Upgrade Restrictions:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual stack support is only available for new clusters. Existing single-stack clusters cannot be upgraded to dual stack.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Network Plugin Compatibility:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual stack support is currently only available with the Kubenet network plugin. Azure CNI does not support dual stack.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Service Type Limitations:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Not all service types support dual stack. For example, ExternalName services do not support dual stack.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Load Balancer Limitations:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Azure Load Balancers used with dual stack services must be configured to support both IPv4 and IPv6. This may require additional configuration and considerations.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;IP Address Management:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Proper IP address management is crucial. Ensure that your virtual network and subnets are configured to support both IPv4 and IPv6 address spaces.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Tooling and Ecosystem Support:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Some Kubernetes tools and add-ons may not fully support dual stack configurations. Ensure compatibility with your specific tools and workflows.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Performance Considerations:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual stack configurations may introduce additional complexity and potential performance overhead. Monitor and optimize your cluster performance accordingly.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Security Considerations:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Dual stack environments may require additional security configurations to ensure both IPv4 and IPv6 traffic is properly secured.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;DNS Configuration:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Ensure that your DNS settings support both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses. This includes configuring DNS records and ensuring that your DNS provider supports dual stack.&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Application Compatibility:&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;font-size: 25px;&quot;&gt;Ensure that your applications are compatible with both IPv4 and IPv6. Some legacy applications may not fully support IPv6." style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Architects Daughter;fontSize=25;fontColor=default;labelBackgroundColor=none;html=1;" parent="jg9sSwiCN6oEBZTyevX6-7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-9480" y="-200" width="3010" height="2170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oLPVPFHUQ2T455JdV-RN-7" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 50px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 102);&quot;&gt;AKS Kubenet + Dual-Stack CNI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=35;fontFamily=Architects Daughter;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DArchitects%2BDaughter;" parent="jg9sSwiCN6oEBZTyevX6-7" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="845" y="-210" width="730" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
